        <div class="row">
            
       <div class="col-lg-8">
             <img class="blog-hero-image" src="data:image/webp;base64," alt="Indian Air Force Agniveer Recruitment 2026 Apply Online">
             <div class="blog-content">
                <div class="blog-body">
                    <h1 class="blog-title text-center mb-4">Indian Air Force Agniveer Vayu Recruitment 2026: Application Closed, Exams Approach!</h1>

                    <p class="mb-4">The Indian Air Force (IAF) recently provided a significant opportunity for young, aspiring individuals to join its ranks as Agniveer Vayu under the transformative Agnipath Scheme. While the application window for the Agniveer Vayu Intake 01/2027 has now concluded, candidates who successfully applied are gearing up for the online examination, scheduled for late March 2026. This comprehensive guide details the key aspects of the recruitment, helping both current applicants and those aspiring for future intakes to stay informed and prepared.</p>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Important Dates for Agniveer Vayu Intake 01/2027</h2>
                    <p>It's crucial for candidates to be aware of the key dates that shaped this recruitment cycle:</p>
                    <table>
                      <thead>
                        <tr>
                          <th>Event</th>
                          <th>Dates</th>
                        </tr>
                      </thead>
                      <tbody>
                        <tr>
                          <td>Initial Online Application Start Date</td>
                          <td>January 12, 2026</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                          <td>Initial Online Application Last Date</td>
                          <td>February 08, 2026</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                          <td>Re-opened Application Start Date</td>
                          <td>March 03, 2026</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                          <td>Re-opened Application Last Date</td>
                          <td>March 10, 2026</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                          <td>Online Exam City Intimation</td>
                          <td>March 2026</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                          <td>Admit Card Release</td>
                          <td>24-48 Hours Before Exam</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                          <td>Online Exam Dates</td>
                          <td>March 30-31, 2026</td>
                        </tr>
                      </tbody>
                    </table>

                    <p class="highlight-text"><strong>Note:</strong> As of March 20, 2026, the application window for Agniveer Vayu Intake 01/2027 is now closed. Candidates should focus on preparing for the upcoming online examination.</p>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Understanding the Agnipath Scheme &amp; Agniveer Vayu</h2>
                    <p>The Agnipath scheme is a revolutionary initiative by the Government of India, offering young citizens an opportunity to serve in the armed forces for a tenure of four years as 'Agniveers'. Under this scheme, Agniveer Vayu are enrolled into the Indian Air Force, gaining invaluable military training, discipline, and a chance to contribute to national security. After the four-year engagement, up to 25% of Agniveers may be selected to continue in the regular cadre based on their performance and organizational requirements.</p>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Eligibility Criteria for Agniveer Vayu</h2>
                    <p>Candidates applying for the Agniveer Vayu recruitment must meet specific criteria to be considered eligible.</p>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">1. Age Limit</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">
                            Applicants must be unmarried and born between January 01, 2006, and July 01, 2009 (both dates inclusive). This implies candidates should be between 17.5 to 21 years of age at the time of enrolment.
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">2. Educational Qualification</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">
                            Candidates must possess one of the following qualifications with a minimum of 50% marks in aggregate and 50% marks in English:
                            <ul>
                                <li><strong>For Science Subjects:</strong> Passed Intermediate/10+2/Equivalent examination with Mathematics, Physics, and English. OR Passed a three-year Diploma Course in Engineering (Mechanical/Electrical/Electronics/Automobile/Computer Science/Instrumentation Technology/Information Technology). OR Passed a two-year Vocational Course with non-vocational subjects Physics and Mathematics.</li>
                                <li><strong>For Other than Science Subjects:</strong> Passed Intermediate/10+2/Equivalent examination in any stream/subjects with English. OR Passed a two-year Vocational Course with English.</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">3. Marital Status</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">
                            Only unmarried Indian male and female candidates are eligible to apply. Marriage during the four-year engagement period will lead to discharge.
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">4. Physical and Medical Standards</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">
                            Candidates need to meet prescribed physical and medical standards including:
                            <ul>
                                <li><strong>Height:</strong> Minimum 152.5 cm for males and 152 cm for females (relaxations for specific regions like North East/Hilly Areas/Lakshadweep).</li>
                                <li><strong>Chest:</strong> For males, a minimum of 77 cm with an expansion of 5 cm. For females, a 5 cm expansion is required.</li>
                                <li><strong>Vision:</strong> Correctable to 6/6 in each eye, with specific Colour Vision standards.</li>
                                <li><strong>Other:</strong> Weight proportionate to height and age, strict policy against tattoos in certain areas, and zero tolerance for NDPS.</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <h2 class="section-title">The Selection Process</h2>
                    <p>The selection process for Agniveer Vayu Intake 01/2027 is rigorous and multi-phased to ensure only the most suitable candidates are chosen.</p>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">1. Phase I: Online Test (CBT)</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">
                            An online computer-based test (CBT) will be conducted, evaluating candidates on subjects relevant to their chosen stream (Science or Other than Science). Admit cards for this phase are usually released 24-48 hours before the exam.
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">2. Phase II: Physical Fitness Test (PFT) &amp; Adaptability Test</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">
                            Shortlisted candidates from Phase I will undergo a Physical Fitness Test (PFT) and Adaptability Test. The PFT includes a 1.6 km run within specified times (7 minutes for males, 8 minutes for females), along with push-ups, sit-ups, and squats. Adaptability tests assess suitability for military life.
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">3. Phase III: Medical Examination</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">
                            Candidates who clear Phase II will undergo a comprehensive medical examination by authorized Air Force Medical Teams.
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <h2 class="section-title">How to Apply Online (for Future Intakes)</h2>
                    <p>While the current application window is closed, prospective candidates for future intakes can follow these general steps:</p>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">1. Registration</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">
                            Visit the official Indian Air Force Agniveer recruitment portal (iafrecruitment.edcil.co.in or agnipathvayu.cdac.in). Register using a valid email ID and mobile number.
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">2. Fill Application Form</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">
                            Log in with your credentials and accurately fill in personal, qualification, and declaration details.
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">3. Upload Documents</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">
                            Upload scanned copies of required documents, including your passport-size photograph, signature, and left-hand thumb impression, adhering to specified size and format guidelines. A live image capture via webcam may also be required.
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">4. Pay Application Fee</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">
                            Pay the prescribed application fee (₹550 + 18% GST for Intake 01/2027) through the online payment gateway.
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">5. Submit and Print</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">
                            Submit the completed application form and take a printout for future reference.
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Benefits of an Agniveer Vayu Career</h2>
                    <p>Joining the Indian Air Force as an Agniveer Vayu comes with a host of benefits:</p>
                    <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                        <p>✅ <strong>Attractive Monthly Emoluments:</strong> Agniveers receive a structured monthly package, starting at ₹30,000 in the first year and increasing to ₹40,000 by the fourth year.</p>
                        <p>✅ <strong>"Seva Nidhi" Package:</strong> Upon completion of four years, Agniveers receive a "Seva Nidhi" package of approximately ₹11.71 Lakh (tax-exempt), which includes their contributions and matching contributions from the government, plus accrued interest.</p>
                        <p>✅ <strong>Insurance and Allowances:</strong> They are provided with a non-contributory Life Insurance Cover of ₹48 Lakh and various allowances for risk, hardship, dress, and travel.</p>
                        <p>✅ <strong>Skill Development:</strong> The scheme focuses on enhancing skills, making Agniveers highly employable in various sectors post their tenure.</p>
                        <p>✅ <strong>Opportunity for Permanent Enrolment:</strong> Up to 25% of Agniveers may be selected for permanent enrolment in the Indian Air Force based on merit and organizational requirements.</p>
                    </div>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Special Opportunity: Agniveer Vayu (Sports) Intake 02/2026</h2>
                    <p>For outstanding unmarried male sportspersons, the Indian Air Force has also opened applications for Agniveer Vayu (Sports) Intake 02/2026. This is a distinct recruitment drive with its own timeline.</p>
                    <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                        <p>✅ <strong>Application Window:</strong> March 23 to March 29, 2026.</p>
                        <p>✅ <strong>Recruitment Trials:</strong> April 08 to April 10, 2026, in New Delhi.</p>
                        <p>✅ <strong>Eligibility:</strong> 10+2, Diploma, or Vocational qualified candidates with prescribed national/international sports achievements.</p>
                    </div>
                    <p>Interested sportspersons should visit agnipathvayu.cdac.in between the specified dates to apply.</p>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Looking Ahead</h2>
                    <p>While the application period for the general Agniveer Vayu Intake 01/2027 has concluded, the upcoming online examination presents the next critical phase for applicants. For those who missed this cycle or are planning to join in the future, it is essential to remain vigilant for upcoming notifications and prepare diligently. The Indian Air Force offers a challenging yet rewarding career, fostering discipline, patriotism, and professional growth. Keep an eye on the official IAF recruitment website for all the latest updates regarding future intakes and results.</p>
                </div>
             </div>
       </div>

            
            
